  "id": "Harrow-PL_0383_26",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Conversion of dwelling from a single flat to 2 x 1 bed flats; Installation of door in side elevation; Refuse and cycle storage",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of the lack of family sized homes with three or more bedrooms and its preponderance of smaller 1-bed units, would fail to achieve an appropriate housing mix, having regard to the location of the site and its surroundings as well as the evidence of local need which identifies the need for more larger family sized units and would fail to contribute to the creation of inclusive and mixed communities, contrary to the provisions of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policies H1, H2 and H10 of the London Plan (2021) and policies HO1 and HO2 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal has not demonstrated that there would be adequate space for the storage of waste on site and insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate the ability of the new development to provide adequate waste storage for the future occupiers of the development, and contrary to policy CE1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of its siting in a surface water flood zone and a lack of flood maps and data, has provided insufficient information to demonstrate that the proposed development would be capable of providing safe access and emergency egress for future occupiers of&amp;nbsp; the site, contrary to policy SI 12 of the London Plan (2021) and policy CN3 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
